IMPORT prelude

-- Constitution of the State of Florida, Article VII, section 5(a) -- the limit on a state tax upon the income of natural
-- persons, the reason Florida has no personal income tax.
--
-- SEAT: the individual resident or citizen of Florida. "Do I pay Florida income tax? How much could Florida tax my income?"
--
-- Edition: Fla. Const. art. VII as displayed on Online Sunshine (www.leg.state.fl.us, stylesheet path /constitution/2025/),
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/fla-const-art7.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19).
--
-- This is a SHORT encoding, written so that a Florida resident asking the personal income tax question gets the answer the
-- law gives. No Florida statute levying a tax on the income of natural persons is in the deposited Florida law (NOTES.md
-- finding 1); the corporate income tax (Fla. Stat. ch. 220, s 5(b)) is out of the seat.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Florida Constitution art. VII s 5(a) -- no personal income tax beyond the federal allowance`

-- s 5(a): "NATURAL PERSONS. No tax upon estates or inheritances or upon the income of natural persons who are residents or
-- citizens of the state shall be levied by the state, or under its authority, in excess of the aggregate of amounts which may
-- be allowed to be credited upon or deducted from any similar tax levied by the United States or any state."
-- The ceiling is the aggregate the law of the United States or another state allows to be "credited upon or deducted from" its
-- similar tax on account of a Florida tax: a question of that other law, asked as an input (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN `a natural person who is a resident or citizen of Florida` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate that federal or other state law allows to be credited upon or deducted from its similar tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 5(a) ceiling on a Florida tax on the income of` `a natural person who is a resident or citizen of Florida` `given` `the aggregate that federal or other state law allows to be credited upon or deducted from its similar tax` MEANS
    IF   `a natural person who is a resident or citizen of Florida`
    THEN JUST (max 0 `the aggregate that federal or other state law allows to be credited upon or deducted from its similar tax`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- s 5(a) does not limit a tax on persons who are neither residents nor citizens; s 5(b) is about others

DECLARE `Florida income tax answer` IS ONE OF
    `no Florida statute in the deposited law taxes my income, and s 5(a) would cap any such tax at the federal or state allowance`
    `s 5(a) does not protect me: I am neither a Florida resident nor a Florida citizen`

§ `Questions for the individual`

@export Do I pay Florida state income tax as an individual (Fla. Const. art. VII s 5(a))?
GIVEN `I am a Florida resident or citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a natural person who is a resident or citizen of Florida
GIVETH A `Florida income tax answer`
`Do I pay Florida income tax` MEANS
    IF   `I am a Florida resident or citizen`
    THEN `no Florida statute in the deposited law taxes my income, and s 5(a) would cap any such tax at the federal or state allowance`
    ELSE `s 5(a) does not protect me: I am neither a Florida resident nor a Florida citizen`

@export What is the most Florida could tax my income under its Constitution (art. VII s 5(a))?
GIVEN `I am a Florida resident or citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a natural person who is a resident or citizen of Florida
      `the federal or other state allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc The aggregate amount that federal law or another state's law would allow to be credited against, or deducted from, its own similar tax on account of a Florida income tax, in US dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most Florida could tax my income` MEANS
    `the s 5(a) ceiling on a Florida tax on the income of` `I am a Florida resident or citizen` `given` `the federal or other state allowance`
